===============================================================================
1. Purpose:
===============================================================================

This sample demonstrates how to attach a Python probe module using the
DeepStream service-maker Flow API.

It is the Flow API equivalent of:
  ../../pipeline_api/deepstream_python_probe_app/

The Flow API abstracts pipeline element wiring so that probes are attached
with a single call:

  flow.attach(what="sample_video_probe", name="svp", properties={"font-size": 18})

The "sample_video_probe" Python probe counts vehicles and persons per frame
and overlays the result on the OSD display.

For the full list of available Python probe modules and their parameters see:
  /opt/nvidia/deepstream/deepstream/service-maker/modules/python/README

===============================================================================
2. Usage:
===============================================================================

  $ python3 deepstream_python_probe.py <h264_file>

  To enable end-to-end latency measurement with the measure_latency_probe
  module, set the following environment variable before running:

    $ export NVDS_ENABLE_LATENCY_MEASUREMENT=1

  Note: with RTSP/live sources, both measure_fps_probe and
  measure_latency_probe report valid values (FPS and latency respectively).
